  "step_3": "The decision reason requires consideration of skewness — specifically, the proportion of probability assigned to favorable (positive) outcomes versus unfavorable (zero) outcomes. The individual did not mention skewness or compare the distribution of probabilities across outcomes. Instead, the individual focused on the higher winning probability in B and the desire to receive the highest amount (6000 Euros), which reflects a different reasoning — possibly risk preference or expected value — not skewness. The information considered by the individual (winning probability and maximum payout) does not match the information required by the decision reason (distribution of probabilities across outcomes). Furthermore, the justification (desire to receive the highest amount) does not reflect the rule of preferring the more left-skewed lottery. Therefore, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason. The reasoning process described is inconsistent with the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
