  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on skewness — specifically, preferring a lottery where more probability mass is assigned to favorable outcomes (i.e., a higher win probability or a more left-skewed distribution). The individual does not mention skewness or the shape of the probability distribution. Instead, the reasoning is about preferring a higher monetary gain, regardless of probability. While Lottery B has a higher probability of winning (0.2% > 0.1%), the individual does not evaluate the distribution of probabilities or compare the skewness of the two lotteries. The individual's justification is based on the size of the prize, not on the distributional skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual's reasoning does not reflect the rule of preferring the more left-skewed lottery. The information considered (the prize amount) is different from the information required by the skewness-based reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
